# 6. Main user flows

## Flow 1 — Create property

```txt
1. User opens Properties page
2. User clicks Add Property
3. User enters address and characteristics
4. User saves property
5. Property appears in the list
```

## Flow 2 — Configure utilities

```txt
1. User opens property details
2. User opens Utilities tab
3. User enables utilities for this property
4. User optionally adds custom utility type
5. User saves configuration
```

## Flow 3 — Configure meters

```txt
1. User opens property details
2. User opens Meters tab
3. User adds electricity/water/gas meters
4. User enters provider details and submission method
5. User saves meter configuration
```

## Flow 4 — Create tenant

```txt
1. User opens Tenants page or property agreement form
2. User creates tenant
3. User enters contact information
4. User saves tenant
```

## Flow 5 — Create rental agreement

```txt
1. User opens property details
2. User clicks Create Rental Agreement
3. User selects tenant
4. User enters dates, rent, currency, deposit, payment due day
5. User saves agreement
6. Agreement becomes active
```

## Flow 6 — Monthly cycle

```txt
1. Dashboard shows that meter readings should be requested
2. User copies reminder message and sends it to tenant
3. Tenant sends readings manually via messenger
4. User enters readings in Estate Tracker
5. User marks readings as received from tenant
6. User submits readings to provider website/email
7. User marks readings as submitted to provider
8. User receives utility amounts
9. User creates monthly statement
10. User enters utility amounts
11. App calculates total amount due
12. User generates PDF
13. User copies message and sends PDF to tenant
14. User records payments when they arrive
15. Statement becomes paid when full amount is received
```

## Flow 7 — Record separate rent and utility payments

```txt
1. User opens monthly statement
2. User clicks Add Payment
3. User records rent payment with category RENT
4. User records utilities payment with category UTILITIES
5. App shows paid amount and remaining balance
6. App updates statement status
```

## Flow 8 — Partial rent payment

```txt
1. Expected rent is 18000 UAH
2. Tenant pays 10000 UAH
3. User records payment category RENT amount 10000 UAH
4. App shows rent remaining balance 8000 UAH
5. Statement status becomes PARTIALLY_PAID
6. Tenant later pays 8000 UAH
7. User records second payment category RENT amount 8000 UAH
8. App shows rent as paid
```

