# 11. AI agent rules

The coding agent must follow these rules.

## General rules

```txt
- Do not implement the whole app in one step.
- Always work in small, reviewable tasks.
- Prefer simple MVP implementation over over-engineering.
- Reuse patterns from the existing Expense Tracker app where appropriate.
- Keep business logic separated from UI where possible.
- Add type-safe validation for forms.
- Do not hardcode user-specific data.
- Do not add paid third-party services without approval.
```

## Database rules

```txt
- Every user-owned entity must be scoped by userId where appropriate.
- Do not expose data across users.
- Avoid hardcoded utility columns on statements.
- Use StatementItems for flexible charge rows.
- Use Payment as a separate entity from MonthlyStatement.
- Do not use paymentCategory = PARTIAL.
- Calculate partial payment status based on expected vs paid amount.
```

## UI rules

```txt
- Use Material UI.
- Keep UI clean and practical.
- Prefer tables for lists and tabs for property details.
- Use clear status chips.
- Make primary flows obvious.
- Keep forms simple.
- Optimize for desktop first, but keep layout responsive.
```

